playlist-checker (1.6.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A redirect to an address with a bare "blocked" path segment (for
    example https://cache.example/blocked/index.m3u8) is now recognised as
    "not available"; previously only names such as blocked-region or
    blocked-video were found.
  * A picture that matches a learned "not available" banner is still
    recognised when the banner has a small animation (up to 10 % of the
    picture changing); a real live picture is still rejected.
  * Gzip-compressed HLS answers are decompressed before checking, so the
    playlist and its real video segments are read instead of the compressed
    bytes (reported as a plain HTTP 200 before).

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:48:56 +0300

playlist-checker (1.6.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New option "Black screen (no programme, only a logo) = offline": a
    stream that is still (almost) black 8 seconds later is reported offline,
    counted separately in the result and left out of the saved playlist. It
    needs ffmpeg and is on by default when ffmpeg is installed.
  * The "same picture on several channels" question shows a sharp 640 x 360
    preview of the picture instead of enlarging the small 80 x 45 thumbnail.
  * Picture-check ffmpeg input options are built in one place, so the
    thumbnail and preview always use the same User-Agent, Referer and
    headers.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:27:33 +0300

playlist-checker (1.6.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Saved playlists are safe against line breaks: newlines in an XSPF
    title/location or in a pasted channel/group name are kept on one line,
    so they cannot add channels to the saved file.
  * A login now survives a redirected playlist's relative links and an
    http -> https redirect (never another server); default ports compare
    correctly.
  * HTTP 200 answers that are JSON/text errors are reported offline
    (Geo-blocked when they mention the country/region); a normal M3U at a
    channel address is a playlist, not HLS. HLS is recognised only by a
    real #EXT-X- tag at the start of a line.
  * "Mark as geo-blocked" during a running check is no longer overwritten
    by that check's result; the next check updates it normally.
  * Learned banners with only two fields (fingerprint and brightness,
    from older versions) are kept when settings are loaded.
  * .m3u.gz, .m3u8.gz, .pls.gz and .xspf.gz are found by Open folder, URL
    lists and the file dialog; default save names no longer keep .gz.
  * Windows custom-player commands handle quoted paths and arguments.
  * The picture check skips radio/audio channels (direct audio and
    audio-only HLS); "Find banners" checks video channels only.
  * Duplicate detection no longer lowercases the login/password in URLs.
  * The system-player temporary playlist uses a random name and mode 0600;
    old ones are removed after a day.
  * Recheck status counts only the rechecked channels; a check ending
    during a download gives the progress bar back to the download;
    "Remember ticks" stores the current ticks when switched on; settings
    are written atomically with mode 0600; quitting stops ffmpeg picture
    processes; --option lines are not accepted as channels; pasted
    channels get a sensible default file name; URL pipe headers win over
    #EXTVLCOPT in the player, as in the checker.
  * The program keeps its executable bit.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:12:39 +0300

playlist-checker (1.6.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Addresses with a login (http://user:pass@host/...) work for checks and
    playlist downloads; the login is not sent on to other servers.
  * A server's error message (JSON or text) is no longer added as a
    channel - it is shown in the error message instead.
  * HLS master playlists: if the first quality does not work, up to 3
    qualities are tried before a channel is called offline; a UTF-8 BOM
    no longer makes them fail.
  * Relative links of a redirected playlist use the address it came from.
    Kodi style "url|User-Agent=..." works for playlist downloads too.
  * "Open URL" downloads can be stopped, are cancelled by "Clear list" and
    wait for running downloads; a second URL list waits instead of being
    dropped; the Stop button is reset after "Clear list".
  * Learned banner colours are kept when the program restarts.
  * "Save new playlist" split by group: two groups can no longer write
    the same file, and existing files are only replaced after asking;
    names keep their own date / "Playlist Checker" when those options are
    off; ~/ paths are saved as full paths.
  * A local HLS .m3u8 (a stream, not a channel list) is added as one
    channel; a damaged .m3u.gz is reported as damaged.
  * An #EXTINF without an address no longer passes its group to the next
    channel; HTTP errors show their number ("HTTP 404 Not Found").
  * Hebrew vowel marks (niqqud) and Arabic diacritics stay on their
    letter; the rename dialog shows Hebrew names the right way round.
  * Geo-blocked channels count as checked in the group / playlist lists;
    the URL column title follows the click-to-play option at start.
  * Less memory: only still pictures keep a thumbnail during a check.
  * CSV report: names starting with = + - @ are not run as formulas.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:20:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Better "not available" banner detection by picture:
    - up to 3 frames about 0.8 s apart are taken from one download of the
      stream; a picture that moves (more than 0.6 % of it changes) is live
      TV and is never taken for a banner, so different names of one live
      channel, or two TV studios that look alike, are not grouped any more;
    - a banner that starts with a black frame (fade-in) is now recognised
      (the first frame that is not plain black is used);
    - the colours of the picture are compared too, not only its shape and
      brightness: banners with the same layout but other colours are no
      longer mixed up. Banners learned from now on keep their colours;
      banners learned by older versions still work as before.
  * Speed: ffmpeg is stopped as soon as the picture is seen to move (most
    channels after the 2nd frame), so the picture check costs about the
    same time as before. Works with ffmpeg 4.x (-vsync) and 5.1+
    (-fps_mode).
  * Damaged learned-banner entries in the settings file are ignored.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:20:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.5.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: versions of the same channel (e.g. "כאן 11", "כאן 11 HEVC",
    "כאן 11 כתוביות", "כאן 11 - מקור 2") show the same picture and were
    taken for a "not available" banner. Names and tvg-ids are now compared
    without quality, subtitle and source words (HEVC, HD, 4K, subtitles,
    כתוביות, source / מקור N, backup / גיבוי ...), and such versions count
    as one channel.
  * Before asking about the same picture on several channels, a second
    picture is taken a few seconds later: if it has changed, it is the same
    live programme (e.g. one channel under different names in several
    playlists), not a banner, and nothing is asked or marked.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:40:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.5.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Channels that fail with a temporary server problem (timeout, HTTP 408,
    429, 500, 502, 503, 504, connection reset) are checked a second time
    at the end of the check: a few seconds later, fewer at once and with
    twice the time limit. The check result says "on the 2nd try" or
    "(2 tries)", and the status bar how many worked on the 2nd try.
    Settings -> Try again channels with temporary errors (on by default).
    Permanent errors (404, 403, server not found) are not tried again.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:10:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.5.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: channels with a long rewind window (e.g. 24 hours, AWS CloudFront /
    MediaPackage streams) were reported offline with "HLS segment: HTTP 404".
    Their quality playlists are larger than 1 MB, only part was read and the
    last, cut-off line was taken for the newest video segment. Playlists up
    to 16 MB are now read, and when only part arrives in time only complete
    lines are used.

 -- Anton <anton1978@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:55:00 +0300

playlist-checker (1.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the program did not start when the settings file was damaged or had
    wrong values; such values are now ignored.
  * Fix: playlists saved as "Unicode" (UTF-16, Windows Notepad) were refused.
  * Fix: compressed playlists (.m3u.gz, or sent gzip-compressed by a server)
    were taken for a single stream.
  * Fix: stream addresses with spaces or non-Latin letters (Cyrillic,
    Hebrew) were reported offline although players can play them.
  * Fix: with two or more playlists only the first EPG address was saved;
    all are now kept (comma-separated).
  * Fix: a channel with the same address as another one could miss its
    picture (counter stuck, e.g. "2 / 3").
  * Fix: with the picture check switched off, an old picture could still mark
    a channel as geo-blocked.
  * Fix: with "Deep HLS check" off the picture check used all qualities of
    a stream (slow); it now uses the lowest one.
  * Fix: dragging the mouse across stream addresses played a channel.
  * Faster redraw of big lists when the search is cleared.

